****** REM *************************************************************CTTS0016
       REM SUBROUTINE TO SIMULATE THE CARD TO TAPE CONVERTER AND ALSO   CTTS0017
       REM TO CONVERT ROW BINARY CARDS TO COLUMN BINARY CARDS ON A      CTTS0018
       REM TAPE SUITABLE FOR OFF LINE PUNCHING.                         CTTS0019
       REM CALLING SEQUENCE=  TSX CTTS,4                                CTTS0020
       REM                    PZE STAPE,,BTAPE                          CTTS0021
       REM                    (RETURN ON FIRST HOLLERITH CARD)          CTTS0022
       REM                    (RETURN IF CARD READER IS EMPTY)          CTTS0023
       REM                    (RETURN ON END OF FILE)                   CTTS0024
       REM STAPE IS THE NO OF THE TAPE TO BE USED FOR SIMULATION.       CTTS0025
       REM BTAPE IS THE NUMBER OF THE TAPE THAT ROW CARDS ARE TO BE     CTTS0026
       REM     WRITTEN ON.  USE ZERO IF NO TAPE IS ASSIGNED.            CTTS0027
       REM THE FIRST HOLLERITH RETURN IS USED TO SET ID INTO COL. 73-80 CTTS0028
       REM THE IMAGE OF THE FIRST HOLLERITH CARD IN COLUMN BINARY FORM  CTTS0029
       REM IS LOCATED IN COMMON+4 THRU COMMON+27. AT THIS RETURN,       CTTS0030
       REM TRANSFER ANY TWO WORDS FROM THIS REGION INTO COMMON+92 AND   CTTS0031
       REM COMMON+93 FOR ID ON THE ROW CONVERTED CARDS.  THEN RETURN TO CTTS0032
       REM CTTS BY TRA 0,4.                                             CTTS0033
